,\"liveBlogEndDate\":null},{\"acronym\":\"\",\"blogId\":234019,\"blogImageURL\":\"https://images.shiksha.com/mediadata/images/articles/1782231132phps7J90E.jpeg\",\"blogText1\":null,\"blogTitle\":\"JEE Advanced 2027: Exam Date (May 23), Eligibility OUT, Registration, Syllabus, Previous Year Paper, Preparation, Fees\",\"countryId\":2,\"creationDate\":\"2026-06-23 22:21:20\",\"discussionTopic\":12885177,\"homepageImgURL\":\"/mediadata/images/articles/1782231132phps7J90E_b.jpeg\",\"lastModifiedDate\":\"2026-11-25 17:57:17\",\"noIndex\":0,\"tags\":null,\"url\":\"/engineering/articles/jee-advanced-2027-blogId-234019\",\"userId\":29781649,\"summary\":\"IIT Delhi is the organising institute of JEE Advanced 2027. JEE Advanced 2027 exam will be held on May 23. JEE Advanced 2027 registration will start in April. Candidates can check here JEE Advanced 2027 syllabus, previous year papers and study materials to prepare for the exam.\",\"tagType\":\"exam\",\"liveBlogStartDate\":null,\"liveBlogEndDate\":null},{\"acronym\":\"\",\"blogId\":221876,\"blogImageURL\":\"https://images.shiksha.com/mediadata/images/articles/1790158371phpSKsSiP.jpeg\",\"blogText1\":null,\"blogTitle\":\"GATE Qualifying Marks 2027: Expected Cutoff Predictions, Past Year's Passing Marks Trends\",\"countryId\":2,\"creationDate\":\"2026-02-12 00:46:59\",\"discussionTopic\":12596890,\"homepageImgURL\":\"/mediadata/images/articles/1790158371phpSKsSiP_b.jpeg\",\"lastModifiedDate\":\"2026-11-23 14:08:25\",\"noIndex\":0,\"tags\":null,\"url\":\"/engineering/articles/gate-qualifying-marks-blogId-221876\",\"userId\":2582250,\"summary\":\"IIT Madras will release GATE 2027 qualifying marks for all 30 subjects. Candidates preparing for GATE 2027 exam can check expected GATE cutoff marks, passing marks for CSE, GATE minimum qualifying mark for IITs, IISc, NITs, etc. Read here to know about admission cutoff, GATE 2027 marks vs rank etc.\",\"tagType\":\"exam\",\"liveBlogStartDate\":null,\"liveBlogEndDate\":null},{\"acronym\":\"\",\"blogId\":242091,\"blogImageURL\":\"https://images.shiksha.com/mediadata/images/articles/1789585977php7kVBfP.jpeg\",\"blogText1\":null,\"blogTitle\":\"NIRF Engineering Ranking UP 2026: Top Colleges, Previous Year Rankings, Parameters\",\"countryId\":2,\"creationDate\":\"2026-09-17 09:41:49\",\"discussionTopic\":12995697,\"homepageImgURL\":\"/mediadata/images/articles/1789585977php7kVBfP_b.jpeg\",\"lastModifiedDate\":\"2026-11-13 12:43:39\",\"noIndex\":0,\"tags\":null,\"url\":\"/engineering/articles/nirf-engineering-ranking-up-blogId-242091\",\"userId\":27726061,\"summary\":\"NIRF Engineering Ranking UP 2026: Students can check here list of NIRF 2026 Engineering Ranking Colleges in UP. MoE is expected to release NIRF 2026 rankings for colleges in UP soon. As per previous year's NIRF rankings, IIT Kanpur and IIT BHU was included in the top ranked Engineering colleges. Read to know more about NIRF Engineering Colleges.\",\"tagType\":\"multi\",\"liveBlogStartDate\":null,\"liveBlogEndDate\":null}],\"anaWidget\":{\"totalNumber\":449,\"listingType\":\"institute\",\"questionsDetail\":{\"11494808\":[{\"answerId\":12952329,\"answerText\":\"<p>MHT-CET is not necessarily the only way, but you should not assume that you can simply take direct admission without any entrance/eligibility requirements.</p>\",\"activityTime\":\"3 months ago\",\"answerOwnerUserId\":75566599,\"questionId\":11494808,\"discussionId\":null,\"aboutMe\":null,\"commentCount\":1,\"msgCount\":1,\"viewCount\":14,\"status\":\"LIVE\",\"userId\":7388054,\"firstname\":\"Atul\",\"lastname\":\"Mishra\",\"creationDate\":\"2025-06-16 12:00:19\",\"url\":\"https://ask.shiksha.com/can-i-get-admission-to-sae-sinhgad-academy-of-engineering-b-e-b-tech-course-without-mht-cet-qna-11494808\",\"title\":\"Can I get admission to SAE - Sinhgad Academy of Engineering B.E. / B.Tech course without MHT CET? \",\"answerOwnerName\":\"Shariek Sheik\",\"answerOwnerLevel\":\"Beginner-Level 2\",\"answerOwnerImage\":\"\",\"likeCount\":0,\"dislikeCount\":0,\"threadStatus\":null,\"answerCount\":1,\"questionCreationDate\":\"a year ago\",\"hasUserVotedUp\":false,\"hasUserVotedDown\":false,\"isUserFollowing\":false,\"hasUserAnswered\":false,\"type\":\"Q\",\"uniqueId\":null,\"followerCount\":0,\"tags\":[{\"tagId\":192347,\"tagName\":\"IIT Kanpur - Indian Institute of Technology\",\"tagType\":\"Colleges\"},{\"tagId\":928767,\"tagName\":\"SAE - Sinhgad Academy of Engineering\",\"tagType\":\"Colleges\"}]}],\"12831371\":[{\"answerId\":12831403,\"answerText\":\"<p>The<strong> IIT Kanpur MSc cutoff 2026 </strong>was published for round 1 for various All India categories, including the OBC category. For this category, the round 1 cutoff ranged from <strong>155 </strong>to <strong>1134</strong>, wherein<strong> M.Sc. in Statistics </strong>was the most sought-after course. </p><p> Students can refer to the table below to know the<strong> IIT Kanpur cutoff 2026</strong> for various branches, listed from most to least competitive. </p><table style=\\\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9795%; height: 195.889px;\\\" border=\\\"1\\\"><colgroup><col style=\\\"width: 59.6006%;\\\"><col style=\\\"width: 40.3815%;\\\"></colgroup><tbody><tr style=\\\"height: 16.7778px;\\\"><th style=\\\"height: 16.7778px;\\\">Course</th><th style=\\\"height: 16.7778px;\\\"><strong>IIT Kanpur cutoff 2026</strong></th></tr><tr style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\"><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" width=\\\"355\\\" height=\\\"19\\\">M.Sc. in Statistics</td><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" align=\\\"right\\\" width=\\\"64\\\">155</td></tr><tr style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\"><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" height=\\\"19\\\">M.Sc. in Economics</td><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" align=\\\"right\\\">202</td></tr><tr style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\"><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" height=\\\"19\\\">M.Sc. in Physics</td><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" align=\\\"right\\\">203</td></tr><tr style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\"><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" height=\\\"19\\\">M.Sc. in Chemistry</td><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" align=\\\"right\\\">279</td></tr><tr style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\"><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" height=\\\"19\\\">M.Sc. in Mathematics</td><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" align=\\\"right\\\">338</td></tr><tr style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\"><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" height=\\\"19\\\">M.Sc.+ Ph.D. in Physics</td><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" align=\\\"right\\\">417</td></tr><tr style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\"><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" height=\\\"19\\\">M.Sc.+ Ph.D. in Chemistry</td><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" align=\\\"right\\\">504</td></tr><tr style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\"><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" height=\\\"19\\\">Integrated Ph.D. in Sustainable Energy Engineering</td><td style=\\\"height: 22.3889px;\\\" align=\\\"right\\\">1134</td></tr></tbody></table><p> </p>\",\"activityTime\":\"6 months ago\",\"answerOwnerUserId\":97214830,\"questionId\":12831371,\"discussionId\":null,\"aboutMe\":null,\"commentCount\":1,\"msgCount\":1,\"viewCount\":8,\"status\":\"LIVE\",\"userId\":97214830,\"firstname\":\"Neerja Rohatgi\",\"lastname\":null,\"creationDate\":\"2026-05-26 13:26:33\",\"url\":\"https://ask.shiksha.com/what-is-the-iit-kanpur-msc-cutoff-for-obc-qna-12831371\",\"title\":\"What is the IIT Kanpur MSc cutoff for OBC? \",\"answerOwnerName\":\"Neerja Rohatgi \",\"answerOwnerLevel\":\"Contributor-Level 10\",\"answerOwnerImage\":\"\",\"likeCount\":0,\"dislikeCount\":0,\"threadStatus\":null,\"answerCount\":1,\"questionCreationDate\":\"6 months ago\",\"hasUserVotedUp\":false,\"hasUserVotedDown\":false,\"isUserFollowing\":false,\"hasUserAnswered\":false,\"type\":\"Q\",\"uniqueId\":null,\"followerCount\":0,\"tags\":[{\"tagId\":192347,\"tagName\":\"IIT Kanpur - Indian Institute of Technology\",\"tagType\":\"Colleges\"},{\"tagId\":408,\"tagName\":\"M.Sc\",\"tagType\":\"Course synonym\"}]}],\"12874941\":[{\"answerId\":12874953,\"answerText\":\"<p data-pm-slice=\\\"0 []\\\">Students who fulfil the preset eligibility criteria can apply for the PDVVCOE BE course. The eligibility required for the programme is to pass Class 12 with a minimum aggregate of 45% marks from any recognised board of education. The programme application process is online.</p>\",\"activityTime\":\"5 months ago\",\"answerOwnerUserId\":102233514,\"questionId\":12874941,\"discussionId\":null,\"aboutMe\":null,\"commentCount\":1,\"msgCount\":1,\"viewCount\":3,\"status\":\"LIVE\",\"userId\":102233514,\"firstname\":\"Anjali\",\"lastname\":\"Sharma\",\"creationDate\":\"2026-06-17 17:50:58\",\"url\":\"https://ask.shiksha.com/who-can-apply-for-padmashri-dr-vithalrao-vikhe-patil-college-of-engineering-be-btech-qna-12874941\",\"title\":\"Who can apply for Padmashri Dr. Vithalrao Vikhe Patil College of Engineering BE/BTech? \",\"answerOwnerName\":\"Anjali Sharma\",\"answerOwnerLevel\":\"Contributor-Level 10\",\"answerOwnerImage\":\"\",\"likeCount\":0,\"dislikeCount\":0,\"threadStatus\":null,\"answerCount\":1,\"questionCreationDate\":\"5 months ago\",\"hasUserVotedUp\":false,\"hasUserVotedDown\":false,\"isUserFollowing\":false,\"hasUserAnswered\":false,\"type\":\"Q\",\"uniqueId\":null,\"followerCount\":0,\"tags\":[{\"tagId\":2288409,\"tagName\":\"College of Engineering\",\"tagType\":\"Colleges\"},{\"tagId\":192347,\"tagName\":\"IIT Kanpur - Indian Institute of Technology\",\"tagType\":\"Colleges\"}]}],\"12840905\":[{\"answerId\":12957637,\"answerText\":\"<p>Students do not need to wait until 2028. Students from the 2024–2028 batch can appear for IIT JAM 2027 while in their final year (3rd year). It will make them eligible for admission to MSc Economics in 2027.</p>\",\"activityTime\":\"3 months ago\",\"answerOwnerUserId\":99457524,\"questionId\":12840905,\"discussionId\":null,\"aboutMe\":null,\"commentCount\":1,\"msgCount\":1,\"viewCount\":17,\"status\":\"LIVE\",\"userId\":107543006,\"firstname\":\"Vinay\",\"lastname\":\"Verma\",\"creationDate\":\"2026-05-31 13:12:13\",\"url\":\"https://ask.shiksha.com/can-bsc-agriculture-hons-2024-ndash-2028-students-get-admission-to-msc-economics-through-iit-jam-in-2027-or-do-qna-12840905\",\"title\":\"Can BSc Agriculture (Hons) 2024&ndash;2028 students get admission to MSc Economics through IIT JAM in 2027, or do they have to wait until 2028?\",\"answerOwnerName\":\"Akanksha Yadav\",\"answerOwnerLevel\":\"Contributor-Level 10\",\"answerOwnerImage\":\"\",\"likeCount\":0,\"dislikeCount\":0,\"threadStatus\":null,\"answerCount\":1,\"questionCreationDate\":\"5 months ago\",\"hasUserVotedUp\":false,\"hasUserVotedDown\":false,\"isUserFollowing\":false,\"hasUserAnswered\":false,\"type\":\"Q\",\"uniqueId\":null,\"followerCount\":0,\"tags\":[{\"tagId\":192347,\"tagName\":\"IIT Kanpur - Indian Institute of Technology\",\"tagType\":\"Colleges\"},{\"tagId\":799491,\"tagName\":\"M.Sc Economics\",\"tagType\":\"Course substreams\"}]}],\"11423844\":[{\"answerId\":12758051,\"answerText\":\"<div><div data-turn-id-container=\\\"request-69d50ffd-a04c-83a6-8787-cfcb4e9aed40-6\\\" data-is-intersecting=\\\"true\\\"><section dir=\\\"auto\\\" data-turn-id=\\\"request-69d50ffd-a04c-83a6-8787-cfcb4e9aed40-6\\\" data-testid=\\\"conversation-turn-176\\\" data-scroll-anchor=\\\"true\\\" data-turn=\\\"assistant\\\"><div><div><div><div dir=\\\"auto\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\" data-message-author-role=\\\"assistant\\\" data-message-id=\\\"43c2a958-fb70-4c43-8f27-c4a0f1815a83\\\" data-message-model-slug=\\\"gpt-5-3\\\" data-turn-start-message=\\\"true\\\"><div><div><p data-start=\\\"0\\\" data-end=\\\"257\\\">At Lovely Professional University, admission to B.Tech Electrical Engineering is not based on a fixed rank cutoff like many government colleges. LPU mainly considers your performance in LPUNEST, JEE Main, or your 12th marks, along with eligibility criteria.</p><p data-start=\\\"259\\\" data-end=\\\"522\\\">So if you are talking about a rank like 2370, it doesn't directly decide your admission at LPU. Instead, what matters is whether you meet the basic eligibility, which is usually around 60% in 12th with PCM, and how you perform in LPUNEST if you choose that route.</p><p data-start=\\\"524\\\" data-end=\\\"828\\\">With a decent academic background or entrance performance, getting Electrical Engineering at LPU is generally not very difficult because the intake is flexible compared to highly competitive colleges. In fact, such a rank can even help you get a good scholarship if it is from a recognised entrance exam.</p><p data-start=\\\"830\\\" data-end=\\\"1005\\\" data-is-last-node=\\\"\\\" data-is-only-node=\\\"\\\">So overall, yes, you can easily get B.Tech in Electrical Engineering at LPU if you meet the eligibility, and your rank can also help in reducing your fee through scholarships.</p></div></div></div></div><div><div tabindex=\\\"-1\\\" role=\\\"group\\\" aria-label=\\\"Response actions\\\"> </div></div><div><div> </div></div></div></div></section></div></div>\",\"activityTime\":\"7 months ago\",\"answerOwnerUserId\":77038745,\"questionId\":11423844,\"discussionId\":null,\"aboutMe\":null,\"commentCount\":1,\"msgCount\":1,\"viewCount\":19,\"status\":\"LIVE\",\"userId\":47250451,\"firstname\":\"Ritu\",\"lastname\":null,\"creationDate\":\"2025-06-03 00:12:46\",\"url\":\"https://ask.shiksha.com/can-i-get-b-tech-in-electrical-engineering-with-2370-rank-qna-11423844\",\"title\":\"Can I get B.Tech in Electrical Engineering with 2370 rank?\",\"answerOwnerName\":\"Vridhi \",\"answerOwnerLevel\":\"Contributor-Level 7\",\"answerOwnerImage\":\"\",\"likeCount\":0,\"dislikeCount\":0,\"threadStatus\":null,\"answerCount\":1,\"questionCreationDate\":\"a year ago\",\"hasUserVotedUp\":false,\"hasUserVotedDown\":false,\"isUserFollowing\":false,\"hasUserAnswered\":false,\"type\":\"Q\",\"uniqueId\":null,\"followerCount\":0,\"tags\":[{\"tagId\":192347,\"tagName\":\"IIT Kanpur - Indian Institute of Technology\",\"tagType\":\"Colleges\"},{\